# Yalla Nghanni

Bilingual Arabic/English maqam ear-training app. Kotlin + Jetpack Compose, single `:app` module.
Read `AGENTS.md` before making changes.

Key rules:

- Keep `game/RecognitionEngine.kt` pure Kotlin (no Android imports) and covered by unit tests.
- Maqams, lessons, onboarding, and all display copy come only from the generated content pack;
  never hardcode them in Kotlin. Edit `site/public/data/maqams.json` and regenerate with
  `python3 tools/sync_app_pack.py`.
- Arabic is the default language and English is a full translation. Every content field and string
  resource needs both versions; verify RTL and LTR at 320 dp.
- Lesson audio and notation stream from the site; only bundled phrases and the drone ship in the APK.
- Ads only on Home (banner), cold start (app open, once a day), after Results is dismissed (every
  third lesson), and a rewarded 50/50 hint on 3+ option questions. Never during playback, feedback,
  Results, lessons, or onboarding. All ad loading needs UMP consent.
- Never commit real AdMob IDs, keystores, or credentials; builds default to Google test unit IDs.
- User-facing strings go in `res/values/strings.xml` and `res/values-en/strings.xml`.
- Verify with `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest`, `:app:assembleDebug`, and `:app:lintDebug`;
  run `:app:connectedDebugAndroidTest` for UI changes.
